  "documentation": {
    "range": "<p>The millipede species <em>Archispirostreptus gigas</em> is widely distributed across eastern Africa, where it was reported from South Africa, Mozambique, Tanzania, Zanzibar, Kenya and Somalia. It was reported from the Kruger National Park, between Punda Maria and Shingwedzi, as well as from Letaba in South Africa, Tette in Mozambique and Tsavo and Ngaia Forest in Kenya. The exact localities in the other countries are unknown (M. Hamer pers. comm. 2017). However, the known localities suggest a distribution mostly along the east coast of Africa (Mwabvu <em>et al</em>. 2010) and mostly within forests. Although the exact extent of occurrence (EOO) and area of occupancy (AOO) are unknown, both are likely to exceed the thresholds for the Vulnerable category by far. </p>",
    "population": "<p>The population size and trend are unknown.</p>",
    "habitats": "<p>In South Africa, the species is known to inhabit mopane basalt shrubland, but may also be associated with other savanna habitats. Along the eastern coast, it seems to mainly occur in forests (M. Hamer pers. comm. 2017).</p>",
    "threats": "<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">As the exact distribution in several countries is unknown, it is not possible to determine the threats occurring to the species in those parts of the distribution range. However, habitat loss due to the conversion of natural vegetation for agricultural purposes and housing development is likely to influence the species in part of its wide distribution range. Furthermore, individuals of the species are collected for the international pet trade, but the extent and impact of this are unknown (M. Hamer pers. comm. 2017).</p>",
    "measures": "<p>No species-specific conservation measures are in place. The species occurs in the Kruger National Park. Research is needed to determine the exact distribution and habitat requirements of the species as well as its population size and trend.</p>",
    "use_trade": "The species is present in the international pet trade. However, the extent and impact of the collection of wild specimens is unknown.",
    "rationale": "<p>The millipede species <em>Archispirostreptus gigas</em> is widely distributed across coastal eastern Africa. With an occurrence reaching from Somalia to South Africa, it is not threatened by extinction. This millipede species is thus assessed Least Concern.</p>",
    "trend_justification": null,
    "taxonomic_notes": null
  },
